      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg. It's also well above the usual 400\u2013800 mg per dose. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **1600 mg per day total**, for example 400 mg by mouth four times daily.\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day and a common upper-range anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the absolute maximum and is rarely used.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order documenting the rationale."
      }
     ],
